OpenSSL 3.5.9 (LTS)

Prebuilt static libs built locally from source via Conan `openssl/3.5.9`
(recipe rev e9977d17028841f6971240542d1f7b11), MSVC 195 / Release / static
/ compiler.runtime=static (i.e. /MT):

- arm64 (armv8): package 577f8200aa77f9cb2e3419022a74d0266213a49f
  (no_asm=False; built 2026-10-29 with clang-cl from LLVM for ARM64 asm)
- x64 (x86_64): package d31d4f52ff48524e357199f07ae106c8444fe942
  (no_asm=False; built 2026-10-29)
- x86 (ia32): package 2a9cab3080eae95c40aaa1d5e4b085d85dbda774
  (no_asm=False; local cache build 2026-10-23)

Why local builds: ConanCenter ships only compiler.runtime=dynamic prebuilts
for 3.5.9; the static-runtime (/MT) variants must be compiled from source.
Mars modules are compiled with /MT (see hook/build.dart) to match upstream
mars/comm/utils.cmake, so OpenSSL must use the static runtime as well to
avoid MSVC CRT mismatch at link time.

Build command (per arch, run inside a VS x64 dev shell with LLVM on PATH
for arm64 asm):
  conan install --requires=openssl/3.5.9 --build=missing \
    -s:h os=Windows -s:h arch=<armv8|x86_64|ia32> -s:h compiler=msvc \
    -s:h compiler.version=195 -s:h compiler.runtime=static \
    -s:h compiler.runtime_type=Release -s:h build_type=Release \
    -s:b os=Windows -s:b arch=armv8 -s:b compiler=msvc \
    -s:b compiler.version=195 -s:b compiler.runtime=dynamic \
    -s:b compiler.runtime_type=Release -s:b build_type=Release

Version policy: OpenSSL 3.5 is the current LTS release (supported until
2030-04-08). OpenSSL 3.6 is NOT an LTS release (support ends 2026-11-01)
and must not be used.

Headers: identical across archs except `configuration.h` (per-arch);
the vendored tree uses a dispatcher (configuration.h) selecting
configuration_windows-arm64.h / configuration_windows-x86_64.h.

Mars uses only rand.h / md5.h / crypto.h (RAND_bytes, MD5), which are
stable across 3.x; the build is verified end-to-end (dart test).
